.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-ENV 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-env
.Nd record the environment of a run in the data record
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis env
.Op Fl -rng Ar kind Op Fl -seed Ar seed
.Op Fl -lock Ar file ...
.Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis env
sets the
.Cm env
member of the data record of
.Ar dir
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5 :
.Cm os
and
.Cm arch
(those this tool was built for),
.Cm noqtis
(its version),
.Cm locale
.Pf ( Ev LC_ALL ,
else
.Ev LANG )
and
.Cm tz
.Pq Ev TZ ,
when set;
.Cm rng
from
.Fl -rng
and
.Fl -seed ;
and
.Cm locks :
the SHA-256 of each lock file named with
.Fl -lock
(a path in
.Ar dir ,
up to 32), or else of each of
.Pa renv.lock ,
.Pa uv.lock ,
.Pa poetry.lock ,
.Pa Pipfile.lock ,
.Pa requirements.txt ,
.Pa Cargo.lock ,
.Pa go.sum ,
.Pa package-lock.json ,
.Pa pnpm-lock.yaml ,
.Pa yarn.lock ,
.Pa environment.yml
and
.Pa Manifest.toml
found at the top of
.Ar dir .
It replaces the
.Cm env
there.
The language runtime and its packages
.Pq Cm runtime
are filled by a binding, which knows them, with
.Cm noqtis data put .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the record is written, 2 on a usage or file error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-diff 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
